# Foundation image, built with the repository root as context.
# This file takes precedence over the inference-oriented root .dockerignore.
# The image needs the lock and six source files; everything else would only make the build
# context (a Dropbox tree with the lab's data in it) enormous.
**
!docker/requirements-foundation.txt
!eforecast/__init__.py
!eforecast/runtime_contract.py
!eforecast/image_runtime.py
!eforecast/profile_runtime.py
!eforecast/profile_policy.py
!eforecast/runtime_adapters
!eforecast/runtime_adapters/**

# Named although the rules above already exclude them. The allow-list is what keeps the private
# cases, the credentials and the trained output out of this context, and an allow-list is one
# careless '!eforecast/**' away from carrying all three. These lines come last, so they win.
configuration/cases
configuration/config*.py
eforecast/nwp_extraction/openweather_key.json
**/__pycache__
**/lightning_logs
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pickle
**/*.pkl
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.ckpt
**/*.log
